{"created": "2022-09-27T15:35:12.398344+00:00", "modified": "2023-03-21T16:31:17.828972+00:00", "id": 7114558, "conceptrecid": "7114557", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7114558", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.7114557", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7114558", "metadata": {"title": "CellPainting-CNN model", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7114558", "publication_date": "2022-09-26", "description": "<p>The supplementary model for the publication &quot;<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1101/2022.08.12.503783\">Learning representations for image-based profiling of perturbations</a>&quot;, if you use this model, please cite our publication.</p>\n\n<p>It was trained on images of single-cells obtained with Cell Painting assay (488 treatments and 2 negative controls from 5 source datasets). The architechture used is EfficientNet.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>You can find instructions specifically related on profiling with this model <a href=\"https://cytomining.github.io/DeepProfiler-handbook/docs/06-profiling.html#profiling-with-cell-painting-cnn-model\">in our DeepProfiler handbook</a>.&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>We recommend to use this model with <a href=\"https://github.com/cytomining/DeepProfiler\">DeepProfiler software</a>.&nbsp;It is possible to use this model separately, but your Python environment should have the following package installed:&nbsp;</p>\n\n<pre><code>efficientnet==1.1.1</code></pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Nikita Moshkov", "affiliation": "Biological Research Center, Szeged, Hungary", "orcid": "0000-0002-5823-4884"}, {"name": "Michael Bornholdt", "affiliation": "Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard"}, {"name": "Santiago Benoit", "affiliation": "Carnegie Mellon University"}, {"name": "Matthew Smith", "affiliation": "Harvard College"}, {"name": "Claire McQuin", "affiliation": "Broad Institute of MIT and Harvard"}, {"name": "Allen Goodman", "affiliation": "Meta", "orcid": "0000-0002-6434-2320"}, {"name": "Rebecca Senft", "affiliation": "Broad Insti